  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UPSCALING ELEPHANT CONSERVATION EFFORTS IN CENTRAL AND EASTERN NEPAL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to work in partnership with the Department of National Parks and Wildlife Conservation (DNPWC) and local communities to ensure the long-term survival and recovery of the wild Asian elephant population of the central and eastern Terai Arc landscape of Nepal. Project objectives are to: (1) strengthen capacity to respond to and minimize human-elephant conflict; and (2) improve tolerance towards wild elephants through behavior change-focused education and outreach programs. Project activities are to: (1) set up a well-equipped seven-person elephant response team (ERT) to monitor individual problem elephants and provide rapid response to human-elephant conflict (HEC) events; (2) form and strengthen 30 community-based rapid response teams (RRTs) in high-HEC villages who will work in coordination with ERTs to provide rapid response to HEC events; (3) develop a landscape-wide database on HEC for DNPWC to inform and improve policies and management actions; (4) train 50 youths as trainers on human-elephant co-existence (HECx) and mobilize them to organize 150 village-level HECx education sessions; (5) produce and broadcast an FM radio program and distribute posters and education materials on elephants and HEC to schools and the public; and (6) conduct a detailed social survey using focus groups and a semi.structured questionnaire to collect baseline information on attitudes of the community towards elephants and HEC mitigation measures.</narrative>
  </description>
